  "chapter": {
    "number": 32,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(33) A Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Rejoice in the Lord, you⌃ righteous; praise becomes the upright.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 58
          },
          {
            "text": "Praise the Lord on the harp; platy to him on a lute of ten strings.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Sing to him a new song; play skillfully with a loud noise.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the word of the Lord is right; and all his works are",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 59
          },
          {
            "text": "faithful.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He loves mercy and judgment; the earth is full the mercy of the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "By the word of the Lord the heavens were established; and all the host of them by the breath of his mouth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who gathers the waters of the sea as in a bottle; who lays up the deeps in treasuries.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let all the earth fear the Lord; and let all that dwell in the world be moved because of him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he spoke, and they were made; he commanded, and they were created.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord frustrates the counsels of the nations; he brings to nothing also the reasonings of the peoples, and brings to nothing the counsels of princes.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But the counsel of the Lord endures for ever, the thoughts of his heart from generation to generation.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed is the nation whose God is the Lord; the people whom he has chosen for his own inheritance.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord looks out of heaven; he beholds all the sons of men.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He looks from his prepared habitation on all the dwellers on the earth;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "who fashioned their hearts",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 60
          },
          {
            "text": "alone; who understands all their works.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A king is not saved by reason of a great host; and a giant shall not be delivered by the greatness of his strength.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A horse is vain for safety; neither shall he be delivered by the greatness of his power.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Behold, the eyes of the Lord are on them that fear him, those that hope in his mercy;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "to deliver their souls from death, and to keep them alive in famine.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Our soul waits on the Lord; for he is our helper and defender.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For our heart shall rejoice in him, and we have hoped in his holy name.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let your mercy, O Lord, be upon us, according as we have hoped in you.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 58,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Rather, 'confess' or give thanks to.'",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 32,
          "verse": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 59,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Rather, Gr. in or with faithfulness.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 32,
          "verse": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 60,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Perhaps 'individually.' Vulg. sigillatim.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 32,
          "verse": 15
        }
      }
    ]
  },
